SOAPBOX: Operated again as a mobile on Stonington Point in Stonington CT.
SOAPBOX: Other committments and extreme cold weather limited my activity to
SOAPBOX: just a few hours on Friday evening. Used my nominal 21 foot base
SOAPBOX: loaded "DX Skimmer" fixed mobile antenna made from a 2 piece ribbed
SOAPBOX: aluminum telescoping pool skimmer poie and a 4 foot hamstick stinger,
SOAPBOX: supported in a sailboat type mast step in the left rear corner of our
SOAPBOX: 2012 Tacoma 4x4 truck bed. Series L loading and shunt L impedance
SOAPBOX: match at feed point. IC-7100 at 100 watts. No external radials, just
SOAPBOX: the truck body as a counterpoise. Paper logging and duping,
SOAPBOX: transcribed to Cabrillo post contest. High winds from the west coming
SOAPBOX: up 100 miles of Long Island Sound were rocking the truck and
SOAPBOX: appeared to throw off the antenna tuning somewhat as the stinger on
SOAPBOX: top moved around. Also made taking the antenna down at the end of the
SOAPBOX: session interesting, the side load of the antenna tubing in the mast
SOAPBOX: step made it a real chore to pull the antanna out of the step. The
SOAPBOX: mast then became an an insanely heavy light saber to keep control of
SOAPBOX: when it finally popped out of the step!
SOAPBOX: Was concerned about propagation following the big geomnagnetic storm
SOAPBOX: earlier in the week and the associated polar cap absorbrtion radiation
SOAPBOX: storm, but overall signals were failry strong and band noise low.
SOAPBOX: Looking forward to the ARRL DX CW Test!
SOAPBOX: 73 DBF and ZUT de Chris AJ1G
